/**
 * Manrope, as font data the OG card can actually render with.
 *
 * `next/og` rasterizes through Satori, which does NOT inherit the page's CSS
 * fonts — it only draws with font binaries handed to `ImageResponse`, falling
 * back to its bundled Noto Sans otherwise. That fallback is why the social card
 * used to render in a typeface that appears nowhere else in the product, while
 * the app itself is set in Manrope (app/layout.tsx, matching CookPilot).
 *
 * Embedded base64 for the same reason the logo is (see opengraph-image.tsx):
 * `public/` is never bundled into Vercel's serverless function and build
 * tracing didn't reliably include co-located files, so anything read from disk
 * at runtime threw ENOENT in production. A string constant is just JS.
 *
 * Two static instances cut from the Manrope variable font (wght axis 200-800):
 * 400 for body copy, 800 for the wordmark and headline — matching `Wordmark`'s
 * `font-extrabold` in components/Logo.tsx. Satori's variable-font support is
 * unreliable, so these are pinned static cuts rather than one variable file.
 *
 * Subset to printable ASCII plus common typographic punctuation, which keeps
 * each cut around 18KB. Text outside that set will render blank, so if the card
 * ever gains a character beyond it, regenerate. To regenerate: instance the
 * Manrope variable TTF at the target weight with fontTools
 * (`varLib.instancer.instantiateVariableFont`), subset it, and base64 the
 * result. Manrope is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, which permits
 * embedding.
 */

